  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA value remains network-concentrated:</strong> the top chains continue to capture the majority of distributed issuance and often set near-term market direction. Related: <a href=\"https://thedefiant.io/news/tradfi-and-fintech/only-four-of-top-20-crypto-treasury-firms-trade-above-holdings-value-dwf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Only Four of Top 20 Crypto Treasury Firms Trade Above Holdings Value: DWF</a> (The Defiant).</li><li><strong>Institutional expansion is likely staged:</strong> large-scale adoption typically lands on proven networks first, then broadens as compliance, interoperability, and liquidity deepen. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/ecosystems/2026-09-24-solana-foundation-taps-binance-polygon-vets-to-drive-institutional-adoption-and-payments-416254\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Solana Foundation taps Binance, Polygon vets to drive institutional adoption and payments</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Custody and issuance integrations are moving rankings first:</strong> Chains that win custody and issuance integrations usually pull distributed value share before the broader RWA market total catches up. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/magic-eden-nft-whitehat-vulnerability?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Magic Eden scare puts 3,832 NFTs in whitehat protective custody</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
